<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abu Kalijar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1009">1009</a>–1048</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abu Kalijar was a Buyid ruler who governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fars">Fars</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khuzestan">Khuzistan</a> from 1024 and also <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> from 1044 until his death in 1048. One of the last capable members of the dynasty, he reunited much of its southern territory, but his reign was troubled by quarrels with his relatives and by the growing threat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuk Turks</a>, whom his weaker successors could not resist.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abu-kalijar.jpg" alt="Abu Kalijar" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Classical Numismatic Group; [1] · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:AbuKalijarBuyidCoinHistoryofIran.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
